  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the 20 files that make up the export-tracking system's full surface area:\n\n**Schema / model layer**\n- `zerver/models/realm_audit_logs.py` \u2014 current tracking lives here: `AuditLogEventType.REALM_EXPORTED` (206) + the `extra_data` JSONField on `RealmAuditLog` that stores `export_path`, `started_timestamp`, `failed_timestamp`, `deleted_timestamp`. This is what `RealmExport` replaces.\n- `zerver/models/__init__.py` \u2014 model registration point; needs the new `RealmExport` import/export added.\n\n**Direct references**\n- `zerver/actions/realm_export.py` \u2014 `notify_realm_export`, `do_delete_realm_export` (reads/writes `extra_data`).\n- `zerver/views/realm_export.py` \u2014 `export_realm`, `get_realm_exports`, `delete_realm_export` endpoints; creates the `RealmAuditLog` row and reads `extra_data` directly.\n- `zerver/lib/export.py` \u2014 `get_realm_exports_serialized` (builds the API-facing dict from `extra_data`) and `export_realm_wrapper`/`do_export_realm`.\n\n**Indirect references (the \"tentacles\")**\n- `zerver/worker/deferred_work.py` \u2014 the `realm_export` background job; reads/writes `extra_data` at each stage (started/failed/export_path).\n- `zerver/management/commands/export.py` \u2014 CLI export path creates its own `RealmAuditLog` row.\n- `zerver/lib/import_realm.py` \u2014 handles `REALM_EXPORTED` entries during realm import.\n- `zerver/lib/upload/{__init__,base,s3,local}.py` \u2014 `delete_export_tarball` and friends, used by `do_delete_realm_export`.\n- `zproject/urls.py` \u2014 routes `export/realm*` to the views above (unlikely to change, but part of the surface).\n- `zerver/lib/event_schema.py` \u2014 `check_realm_export`/`_check_realm_export`, the schema the `realm_export` event must satisfy.\n\n**Test coverage**\n- `zerver/tests/test_realm_export.py` \u2014 primary dedicated export tests (end-to-end, S3 + local).\n- `zerver/tests/test_import_export.py` \u2014 round-trip tests referencing `REALM_EXPORTED`.\n- `zerver/tests/test_events.py` \u2014 event-schema tests for the `realm_export` event.\n- `zerver/tests/test_management_commands.py` \u2014 CLI `export` command tests.\n- `zerver/tests/test_upload_s3.py`, `zerver/tests/test_upload_local.py` \u2014 `delete_export_tarball` coverage per storage backend.\n\nNote: `zerver/migrations/0595_add_realmexport_table_and_backfill.py` itself was not found in this checkout \u2014 the codebase's export tracking is still on `RealmAuditLog.extra_data` (not a JSON file on disk as the ticket describes), so that migration appears not yet present in this snapshot. Flag this discrepancy before writing `SCHEMA_IMPACT.md`.",
